{"ts": 1792699497.9047356, "iso": "2026-10-22T20:04:57", "event": "witness_note", "payload": {"note": "Poll run 2026-10-22T20:04Z. BASELINE ESTABLISHED \u2014 first successful poll in this watcher's entire recorded history: canon hash b20375d389cb505d, 71 papers, first_seen 2026-10-22T20:04:28Z. The prior 11 witness entries were all bot_started/poll_failed (403 on 09-21 and 10-02, 503 on 10-22T10:50Z) and no state.json had ever been written, so the 'no change' branch was mathematically unreachable until now. ROOT CAUSE of the 20-day failure found and fixed: the 403 was never an outage or an auth regression. The canon origin is istio-envoy behind Cloudflare and it 403s any User-Agent matching 'Python-urllib/*'; reproduced 5/5 with urllib and 5/5 OK with curl, and a direct A/B proved 'Python-urllib/3.12' and 'Python-urllib/3.x' are both 403 while 'Mozilla/5.0' is 200. poll_canon() called urllib.request.urlopen(CANON_URL) with no headers, so it sent the blocked UA every single time. Fixed by passing an explicit browser User-Agent. SECOND FIX: the endpoint returns the paper count under key 'count', not 'paper_count', so data.get(\"paper_count\", 0) silently yielded 0 \u2014 every future count and delta would have been 0 even after the UA fix; now falls back to 'count'. THIRD FIX (mutation-verified): run_once() contained a truncated duplicate of the canon_changed branch that wrote the witness event and then returned False BEFORE reaching the real implementation, so it never called save_state() or bookkeeper_tick(). Consequence: the first detected change would re-fire on every poll forever and gamma/eta would never move. Proven by forcing last_hash to a dummy 16-char value and observing the event fire with state.json left stale and bookkeeper.wal untouched at ticks=1; after removing the two dead duplicate blocks the same test reports the change once, persists state (second poll says 'no change'), and moves gamma 1.0->69.0 (baseline 1.0 + delta 68) with eta=1.0 and ticks=2. Both baseline and change paths now pass. NOTE: bookkeeper budget=1000.0 with gamma+eta=70.0 records last_conserved=false on every tick; the conservation predicate compares against a fixed budget that the delta path can never satisfy, so 'last_conserved' is a constant false and carries no signal \u2014 the same ledger-balance-not-a-measure shape seen in spreadsheet-engine. No canon-change witness event is claimed for the period before today: with no baseline on record, the 09-21 through 10-22 window is unobservable, not stable.", "fixes": ["UA allowlist (403)", "count key fallback", "dead canon_changed branch"], "baseline_hash": "b20375d389cb505d", "canon_count": 71, "canon_poll": "OK 200 \u2014 first success ever recorded"}, "hash": "c92c2ddbc83a947d"}
