ication. SUBSTRATE TRUNCATION TRAP, re-verified live this run rather than assumed: a 'cp' of substrate-witness.jsonl and topics.json to the NAS returned 'failed to close ... Disk quota exceeded' and landed as 0-byte stubs that still appeared in ls -la with nonzero-looking names; fixed without touching the script by symlinking the two NAS target files to their /tmp/wm-run/bots/substrate-bus/ counterparts, with read-through confirming 660 and 4508 bytes. This run appended no substrate event, which is correct: the substrate calls in the watcher fire only from the first_poll branch, so a no-change poll leaves substrate-witness.jsonl byte-unchanged (md5 1a9289b50aef536c4736816ad32bc3dc, 660 bytes). CARRIED FORWARD, still PROVEN rather than merely reported: the bookkeeper budget=1000.0 vs gamma+eta=70.0 defect. The predicate abs(gamma+eta-budget) < 1e-6 or (delta_gamma==0 and delta_eta==0) has an UNREACHABLE (0,0) escape clause on every call path (first_poll always passes delta_gamma=1.0; canon_changed always passes delta_eta=1.0), and the first clause can only pass if the running total hits EXACTLY 1000.0 within 1e-6, which is a coincidence target rather than a conservation law. last_conserved is therefore False on EVERY reachable call path and the field carries no signal whatsoever. Thirteenth poll reporting this; still unfixed. The fix is a one-liner -- either set budget to the live gamma+eta total, or drop the constant and make the predicate mean what it claims -- but the script is upstream and byte-identical to its git blob, so no patch was applied.", "canon_poll": "OK 200 -- no change vs 2026-10-22T20:04Z baseline (stable ~24.2h)", "baseline_hash": "b20375d389cb505d", "canon_count": 71, "canon_changed": false, "verified_by": "watcher poll_canon() + independent curl probe before AND after the run (HTTP 200, 13720 bytes, sha256(json, sort_keys)[:16] match)", "script_md5": "206682962c06f9814a5db65c2fbc7267", "upstream_clone_head": "ca4f83b", "witness_rows": 50, "inheri