ngside it or the import dies. Staged script md5 206682962c06f9814a5db65c2fbc7267, byte-identical to upstream; no code changes were needed this run. Because this run used a real sparse git clone rather than the contents API, the NAS quota trap did not apply: /workspace had space, so no symlink shim was needed for the substrate-bus write targets, and the substrate files were read straight from the working tree at their upstream md5s (stat -L, not bare stat, which reports link length not target size). This run appended no substrate event, which is correct. Open defect, still unresolved: bookkeeper uses budget=1000.0 against a gamma+eta total of 70.0, so last_conserved is a constant false by construction - the delta path can never satisfy the predicate, so the field carries no signal. Eighth poll reporting this; still unfixed. Also still open: zero canon_changed events exist in the entire 88-row history, so the canon_changed branch - the only path that exercises substrate_publish(), bookkeeper_tick() and the delta arithmetic - has never executed against live data in this log's lifetime; it is untested code path, and the watcher has so far only ever exercised first_poll, the no-change path, and 6 poll_failed rows."}, "hash": "a938fb09215aea30"}
