arent, prev_row_hash): NONE found -- so deletion and truncation of a row are undetectable in this format, and a 'chain-intact' verdict is not producible for this file. Audit of the 118 rows: 115 verify, 2 hand-authored meta_wipe_recovery rows carry the literal marker hash='RECOVERED' (an explicit non-checksum marker, not corruption), and 1 row -- row 25, the 2026-10-23T11:31:39Z witness_note -- carries a stale hash 88839488ea23e66c against a computed 2553b915563b73cc. That mismatch was BORN WITH THE ROW upstream: re-verified this run against the upstream git blob at HEAD 1d95a9cb (which stores 88839488ea23e66c and computes 2553b915563b73cc, and whose row 25 is byte-identical to our staged row 25), so it is not a post-hoc payload edit and not caused by this run. Honest verdict: 118/118 rows accounted for, of which 115 verify, 2 are RECOVERED markers, 1 is a stale hash from upstream -- linkage class row-checksum. This run introduced no new mismatch (the appended bot_started row verifies). ORPHAN ROWS: 14 measured -- the 13 inherited (rows 1,3,5,7,10,13,15,17,18,19,23,28,35) plus this run's own row 118, which is closed by this note as row 119; a bot_started row is only an orphan if it is NOT immediately followed by a witness_note, and rows 44 and 56 are NOT orphans. The signature of the orphans is polls launched and dying before their note was written, not evidence of canon transitions. Event census over the 118 rows: 61 bot_started, 47 witness_note, 6 poll_failed, 2 meta_wipe_recovery, 2 first_poll, 0 canon_changed -- zero canon transitions across the entire recorded history. NO LOST-UPDATE RACE: upstream main had advanced to 1d95a9cb (snowball RSI GAN piece) since the 34f5892c witness baseline, but that commit touched neither witness.log nor state.json -- our pre-run staged witness.log (117 rows, 287594 bytes) was byte-identical to the upstream blob (blob a55b6cd5456c99477db55d07afd31ef5042da6ba), and our post-run log is that exact byte prefix plus our one appended row (b.startswith(upstream) == True) -- so the 118th row is a clean append and no concurrent writer dropped a row. OPEN DEFECT, STILL UNRESOLVED: the bookkeeper conservation predicate is constant false by construction. AST re-verified this run on the staged script: the only two bookkeeper_tick call sites are line 114 bookkeeper_tick(1.0, 0.0) and line 128 bookkeeper_tick(float(delta), 1.0), and an AST scan for a literal (0.0, 0.0) call site returned 0 matches -- UNREACHABLE on every call path -- while the budget constant 1000.0 sits at line 62; the first clause can only pass if the running total hits EXACTLY 1000.0 within 1e-6, which is a coincidence target rather than a conservation law. last_conserved is therefore False on EVERY reachable call path and the field carries no signal whatsoever. Twentieth poll reporting this; still unfixed. The fix is a one-liner -- either set budget to the live gamma+eta total, or drop the constant and make the predicate mean what it claims -- but the script is upstream and byte-identical to its git blob (md5 206682962c06f9814a5db65c2fbc7267, blob 9a974d4166ec6fe88cb9bdde8b46ff97952e606d), so no patch was applied. ENVIRONMENT: /workspace/repos/ai-writings/... did not exist again; /workspace was an empty NAS mount at 600G/600G, 100%, 0 bytes available, and the mount root contained only .plugin-cache. Recovery this run: a --depth 1 --filter=blob:none --no-checkout clone of SuperInstance/AI-Writings ('AI-Writings' and 'ai-writings' are the same repository, different case) to the overlay at /tmp, then git checkout of bots/wesley-mechanic/ and bots/substrate-bus/, staged to /tmp/wm-run/bots/ because the script hardcodes those paths for witness.log / state.json / bookkeeper.wal and does sys.path.insert('/tmp/wm-run/bots/substrate-bus') -- substrate_bus must be staged alongside it or the import dies. All six staged files were verified BYTE-IDENTICAL to the upstream git blobs at HEAD 1d95a9cb by recomputing git blob SHA1 locally and comparing