un by scanning every payload for linkage keys (prev, prev_hash, parent, prev_row_hash): NONE found -- so deletion and truncation of a row are undetectable in this format, and a 'chain-intact' verdict is not producible for this file. Audit of the 125 rows: 122 verify, 2 hand-authored meta_wipe_recovery rows carry the literal marker hash='RECOVERED' (an explicit non-checksum marker, not corruption), and 1 row -- row 25, the 2026-10-23T11:31:39Z witness_note -- carries a stale hash 88839488ea23e66c against a computed 2553b915563b73cc. That mismatch was BORN WITH THE ROW upstream and is the known upstream authoring slip, not a post-hoc payload edit and not caused by this run. Honest verdict: 125/125 rows accounted for, of which 122 verify, 2 are RECOVERED markers, 1 is a stale hash from upstream -- linkage class row-checksum. This run introduced no new mismatch (the appended bot_started row verifies). ORPHAN ROWS: 15 measured -- the 14 inherited (rows 1,3,5,7,10,13,15,17,18,19,23,28,35,120) plus this run's own row 125, which is closed by this note as row 126; a bot_started row is only an orphan if it is NOT immediately followed by a witness_note, and rows 44 and 56 are NOT orphans. The signature of the orphans is polls launched and dying before their note was written, not evidence of canon transitions. Event census over the 125 rows: 65 bot_started, 50 witness_note, 6 poll_failed, 2 meta_wipe_recovery, 2 first_poll, 0 canon_changed -- zero canon transitions across the entire recorded history. NO LOST-UPDATE RACE: our pre-run staged witness.log (124 rows, 313271 bytes, md5 12dfae237da5c64bce4c1ed652d615ea) was byte-identical to the upstream blob, and our post-run log is that exact byte prefix plus our one appended row (ours.startswith(upstream) == True, 313271 -> 313430 bytes, 159 bytes appended) -- so the 125th row is a clean append and no concurrent writer dropped a row. OPEN DEFECT, STILL UNRESOLVED: the bookkeeper conservation predicate is constant false by construction. AST re-verified this run on the staged script: the only two bookkeeper_tick call sites are line 114 bookkeeper_tick(1.0, 0.0) and line 128 bookkeeper_tick(float(delta), 1.0), and an AST scan for a literal (0.0, 0.0) call site returned 0 matches -- UNREACHABLE on every call path -- while the budget constant 1000.0 sits at line 62 and the predicate at line 71; the first clause can only pass if the running total hits EXACTLY 1000.0 within 1e-6, which is a coincidence target rather than a conservation law. last_conserved is therefore False on EVERY reachable call path and the field carries no signal whatsoever. Twenty-third poll reporting this; still unfixed. The fix is a one-liner -- either set budget to the live gamma+eta total, or drop the constant and make the predicate mean what it claims -- but the script is upstream and byte-identical to its git blob (md5 206682962c06f9814a5db65c2fbc7267), so no patch was applied. ENVIRONMENT: /workspace/repos/ai-writings/... did not exist again; /workspace was an empty NAS mount at 600G/600G, 100% used, 0 bytes available. Recovery this run: the GitHub contents API and a --filter=blob:none --sparse clone were both usable, so the six required files were staged to the /tmp overlay at /tmp/wm-run/bots/ because the script hardcodes those paths for witness.log / state.json / bookkeeper.wal and does sys.path.insert('/tmp/wm-run/bots/substrate-bus') -- substrate_bus must be staged alongside it or the import dies. A plain full clone was rejected: the NAS quota is exhausted and the first clone attempt died with 'close error: Disk quota exceeded' while still appearing in ls; /tmp is not subject to the EDQUOT trap, so the clone was redone there. All six staged files were verified byte-identical to upstream by md5 (script 206682962c06f9814a5db65c2fbc7267, witness.log 12dfae237da5c64bce4c1ed652d615ea, state.json 5ce39812d7f3af41583e4003872b6ef6, substrate_bus.py 6fa03e34e185ca52e3f51356bd76f611, substrate-witness.jsonl 246e49ffbb60922343befef78e15bf4b, topics.json e7d4cb8c41b32a724bfec8b1cc60329b). The NAS 0-byte truncation trap was avoided, not assumed: the six NAS-facing paths were symlinked to their /tmp/wm-run counterparts and stat -L confirms 5805 / 313271 / 92 / 4493 / 1532 / 8987 bytes with upstream-matching md5s read through the symlinks. SUBSTRATE: this run appended no substrate event, which is correct: the substrate calls in the watcher fire only from the first_poll branch, so a no-change poll leaves substrate-witness.jsonl byte-unchanged (md5 246e49ffbb60922343befef78e15bf4b, 1532 bytes) and topics.json byte-unchanged (md5 e7d4cb8c41b32a724bfec8b1cc60329b, 8987 bytes) -- both verified post-run."}, "hash": "bc72e74611bd59c1"}
