s run by scanning every payload for linkage keys (prev, prev_hash, parent, prev_row_hash): NONE found -- so deletion and truncation of a row are undetectable in this format, and a 'chain-intact' verdict is not producible for this file. Audit of the 131 rows: 128 verify, 2 hand-authored meta_wipe_recovery rows carry the literal marker hash='RECOVERED' (an explicit non-checksum marker, not corruption), and 1 row -- row 25, the 2026-10-23T11:31:39Z witness_note -- carries a stale hash 88839488ea23e66c against a computed 2553b915563b73cc. That mismatch was BORN WITH THE ROW upstream and is the known upstream authoring slip, not a post-hoc payload edit and not caused by this run. Honest verdict: 131/131 rows accounted for, of which 128 verify, 2 are RECOVERED markers, 1 is a stale hash from upstream -- linkage class row-checksum. This run introduced no new mismatch (the appended bot_started row verifies). ORPHAN ROWS: 15 measured -- the 14 inherited (rows 1,3,5,7,10,13,15,17,18,19,23,28,35,120) plus this run's own row 131, which is closed by this note as row 132; a bot_started row is only an orphan if it is NOT immediately followed by a witness_note, and rows 44 and 56 are NOT orphans. The signature of the orphans is polls launched and dying before their note was written, not evidence of canon transitions. Event census over the 131 rows: 68 bot_started, 53 witness_note, 6 poll_failed, 2 meta_wipe_recovery, 2 first_poll, 0 canon_changed -- zero canon transitions across the entire recorded history. NO LOST-UPDATE RACE: upstream main is still f1c6b336 (identical to our clone head; no commits have landed since the 10:39Z poll), and our pre-run staged witness.log (130 rows, 337136 bytes, md5 eed67393978637a7e37383bb647cf2f6) was byte-identical to the upstream blob, and our post-run log is that exact byte prefix plus our one appended row (ours.startswith(upstream) == True, 337136 -> 337296 bytes, 160 bytes appended) -- so the 131st row is a clean append and no concurrent writer dropped a row. OPEN DEFECT, STILL UNRESOLVED: the bookkeeper conservation predicate is constant false by construction. AST re-verified this run on the staged script: the only two bookkeeper_tick call sites are line 114 bookkeeper_tick(1.0, 0.0) and line 128 bookkeeper_tick(float(delta), 1.0), and an AST scan for a literal (0.0, 0.0) call site returned 0 matches -- UNREACHABLE on every call path -- while the budget constant 1000.0 sits at line 62 and the predicate at line 71; the first clause can only pass if the running total hits EXACTLY 1000.0 within 1e-6, which is a coincidence target rather than a conservation law. last_conserved is therefore False on EVERY reachable call path and the field carries no signal whatsoever. Twenty-sixth poll reporting this; still unfixed. The fix is a one-liner -- either set budget to the live gamma+eta total, or drop the constant and make the predicate mean what it claims -- but the script is upstream and byte-identical to its git blob (md5 206682962c06f9814a5db65c2fbc7267), so no patch was applied. AST also confirms the no-change path writes no substrate event: the four witness() call sites are line 145 bot_started, line 97 poll_failed, line 109 first_poll and line 120 canon_changed -- none of which is reachable on a stable canon -- so substrate-witness.jsonl and topics.json remain byte-unchanged (md5 246e49ffbb60922343befef78e15bf4b and e7d4cb8c41b32a724bfec8b1cc60329b respectively), both verified post-run. ENVIRONMENT: /workspace/repos/ai-writings/... did not exist again; /workspace was an empty NAS mount at 600G/600G, 100% used, 0 bytes available, and the mount root contained only an empty .plugin-cache. Recovery this run: a --filter=blob:none --no-checkout --depth 50 git clone of SuperInstance/AI-Writings was made to the /tmp overlay (NAS quota is exhausted, so a clone there would die with 'Disk quota exceeded' while still appearing in ls), and the six required files were staged to /tmp/wm-run/bots/ because the script hardcodes those paths for witness.log / state.json / bookkeeper.wal and does sys.path.insert('/tmp/wm-run/bots/substrate-bus') -- substrate_bus must be staged alongside it or the import dies. All six staged files were verified byte-identical to upstream by md5 against the git blobs (script 206682962c06f9814a5db65c2fbc7267, witness.log eed67393978637a7e37383bb647cf2f6, state.json 5ce39812d7f3af41583e4003872b6ef6, substrate_bus.py 6fa03e34e185ca52e3f51356bd76f611, substrate-witness.jsonl 246e49ffbb60922343befef78e15bf4b, topics.json e7d4cb8c41b32a724bfec8b1cc60329b). Two new environment hazards were measured and worked around this run: (a) the NAS write trap is SILENT -- a plain 'printf x > /workspace/probe.txt' returns exit 0 yet leaves a 0-byte file, so exit status alone is not evidence of a durable write; and (b) the /tmp overlay is NOT persistent across tool invocations -- the clone directory vanished between two consecutive bash calls, so the entire clone-stage-run-verify sequence had to be executed inside a single shell invocation driven by a heredoc script. Durable output this run was therefore produced on the /tmp overlay and published to the upstream repo via git rather than left on the NAS.", "canon_poll": "OK 200 -- no change vs 2026-10-22T20:04Z baseline (stable ~38.7h)", "baseline_hash": "b20375d389cb505d", "canon_count": 71, "canon_changed": false, "verified_by": "watcher poll_canon() + independent curl probes BEFORE AND AFTER the run (HTTP 200, 13720 bytes each, bodies byte-identical, sha256(json, sort_keys)[:16] match)", "script_md5": "206682962c06f9814a5db65c2fbc7267", "upstream_clone_head": "f1c6b33", "witness_rows": 131, "inherited_row_audit": "128/128 machine rows verify; 2 RECOVERED markers (rows 9, 12); 1 stale hash (row 25) known upstream authoring slip (stored 88839488ea23e66c, computed 2553b915563b73cc)", "orphan_rows": 15, "orphan_detail": "15 bot_started rows with no immediately-following witness_note (rows 1,3,5,7,10,13,15,17,18,19,23,28,35,120,131); row 131 is closed by this note (row 132); rows 44 and 56 are NOT orphans", "event_census": "131 rows: 68 bot_started, 53 witness_note, 6 poll_failed, 2 meta_wipe_recovery, 2 first_poll, 0 canon_changed", "workspace_status": "NAS mount 100% full, 0 bytes avail, writes silently truncate to 0 bytes; /workspace/repos/ai-writings/... absent; recovered via --filter=blob:none --depth 50 clone to /tmp overlay then staged to /tmp/wm-run (32nd wipe); /tmp overlay non-persistent across tool invocations -- full sequence run in one shell invocation", "open_defect": "bookkeeper budget=1000.0 vs gamma+eta=70.0; (0,0) escape clause AST-proven UNREACHABLE on all call paths (0 literal (0.0,0.0) call sites), so last_conserved is False everywhere and carries no signal"}, "hash": "fbbd75cbf0c4a652"}
